<title>ITALY: ENI sees Brent crude average $19.50 in '97.</title>
<headline>ENI sees Brent crude average $19.50 in '97.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian state-controlled energy group ENI said it expected the price of Brent crude to average $19.50 per barrel in 1997, substantially weaker than the prices of around $23.40 in the last quarter of 1996.</p>
<p>ENI said in a prospectus for the sale of a third tranche of its shares that energy demand in Italy this year was expected to show a modest increase of 0.7 percent on 1996.</p>
<p>--Milan bureau +392 66129507</p>
</text>
